{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Length-2 XXX: determinant contour wave function\n\nThis workbook explores the two-site analogue of the length-1 Baxter-to-wave-function map. Everything is explicit here.\n\nWe use `Qtheta(u)=(u-theta1)(u-theta2)` and\n\n`mu_n(u)=rho_n(u)/(Qtheta(u)Qtheta(u-h))`, with `rho_n(u+h)=rho_n(u)`.\n\nThe two Baxter integrals are denoted `I1,I0` through `t(u)=chi u^2+I1 u+I0`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[u,h,theta1,theta2,lambda,chi,I1,I0,Qtheta,t];\nchi=lambda+1/lambda;\nQtheta[u_]:=(u-theta1)(u-theta2);\nt[u_]:=chi u^2+I1 u+I0;",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. Two periodic measures and self-adjointness\n\nThe simplest cycle basis is `rhoA=1`, `rhoB=Exp[2 Pi i u/h]`. Both are `h`-periodic. Periodicity makes the detailed-balance proof identical for either measure.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[rhoA,rhoB,mu,A,Dcoef];\nrhoA[u_]:=1;\nrhoB[u_]:=Exp[2 Pi I u/h];\nmu[rho_][u_]:=rho[u]/(Qtheta[u]Qtheta[u-h]);\n\nperiodicityChecks=PowerExpand[{\n rhoA[u+h]-rhoA[u],\n rhoB[u+h]-rhoB[u]\n}];\n\nA[u_]:=Qtheta[u];\nDcoef[u_]:=Qtheta[u-h];\nselfAdjointCheck[rho_]:=PowerExpand[FullSimplify[{\n mu[rho][u+h]A[u+h]/mu[rho][u]-Dcoef[u],\n mu[rho][u-h]Dcoef[u-h]/mu[rho][u]-A[u]\n}]];\n\n<|\"periodicity\"->periodicityChecks,\n\"rhoA self-adjointness\"->selfAdjointCheck[rhoA],\n\"rhoB self-adjointness\"->selfAdjointCheck[rhoB]|>",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. A site-localized cycle basis\n\nThe equivalent periodic functions\n\n`rho1=1-Exp[2 Pi i (u-theta2)/h]`,\n`rho2=1-Exp[2 Pi i (u-theta1)/h]`\n\ncancel respectively the poles on the theta2 and theta1 lattices. They are linear combinations of `rhoA,rhoB`. For the scalar-product determinant, or for the diagonal wave-function slice where both rows use the same z, this is an ordinary constant row-basis change. The fully polarized `z1,z2` lift below retains a choice of which cycle is attached to which coordinate.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[rho1,rho2];\nrho1[u_]:=1-Exp[2 Pi I (u-theta2)/h];\nrho2[u_]:=1-Exp[2 Pi I (u-theta1)/h];\n\nlocalizedPeriodicity=PowerExpand[{\n rho1[u+h]-rho1[u],\n rho2[u+h]-rho2[u]\n}];\n\nc1=Exp[-2 Pi I theta1/h];\nc2=Exp[-2 Pi I theta2/h];\ncycleChange={{1,-c2},{1,-c1}};\ncycleChangeDet=Simplify[Det[cycleChange]];\n\ncancellationChecks=PowerExpand[{\n rho1[theta2],rho1[theta2+h],\n rho2[theta1],rho2[theta1+h]\n}];\n\n<|\"periodicity\"->localizedPeriodicity,\n\"cancelled-pole numerators\"->cancellationChecks,\n\"cycle change matrix\"->cycleChange,\n\"cycle change determinant\"->cycleChangeDet|>",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "For generic `Exp[-2 Pi i theta1/h] != Exp[-2 Pi i theta2/h]`, the cycle change is invertible. The determinant changes only by `Det[cycleChange]` when both cycle rows are evaluated at the same kernel/coordinate. This covariance must not be overextended to independently polarized row coordinates.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Four-pole contour brackets\n\nThe denominator has poles at `theta1,theta1+h,theta2,theta2+h`. The residue definition below works for either the delocalized or localized cycles.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "poles={theta1,theta1+h,theta2,theta2+h};\n\nClearAll[bracket];\nbracket[rho_][expr_]:=Simplify[\n Sum[Residue[mu[rho][u]expr,{u,p}],{p,poles}]\n];\n\n(* These show directly that the localized measures have no residues on the\n   unwanted site's two poles. *)\nlocalizedResidueChecks=FullSimplify[{\n Residue[mu[rho1][u],{u,theta2}],\n Residue[mu[rho1][u],{u,theta2+h}],\n Residue[mu[rho2][u],{u,theta1}],\n Residue[mu[rho2][u],{u,theta1+h}]\n}];\n\nlocalizedResidueChecks",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. One-variable contour transforms and their jets\n\nTranslate the Baxter function as at length one: `Qbar(u)=Q(u-h)`. For any cycle define\n\n`F_rho(z)=<z^(u/h)Qbar(u)>_rho`,\n`M_rho(z)=<u z^(u/h)Qbar(u)>_rho`.\n\nThe second object is not independent: `M_rho=D_z F_rho`, where `D_z=h z d/dz`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[Qbar,F,Moment,EulerD,qq,zz];\nEulerD[expr_,zz_]:=h zz D[expr,zz];\n\nF[rho_,zz_,qfun_]:=bracket[rho][zz^(u/h)qfun[u]];\nMoment[rho_,zz_,qfun_]:=bracket[rho][u zz^(u/h)qfun[u]];\n\n(* The identity follows before integration from\n   h z d_z z^(u/h)=u z^(u/h). *)\nkernelMomentIdentity=PowerExpand[\n h zz D[zz^(u/h),zz]-u zz^(u/h)\n];\n\nkernelMomentIdentity",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Candidate two-site wave function\n\nUse the two independent cycles as rows and the zeroth/first moments as columns:\n\n`Psi(z1,z2)=Det[{{F1(z1),D1 F1(z1)},{F2(z2),D2 F2(z2)}}]`.\n\nThis is the polarized two-variable lift. Setting `z1=z2=z` gives the direct replacement of one Q-factor by `z^(u/h)` in the stated scalar-product determinant.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[Psi2,z1,z2,qfun];\nPsi2[rhoa_,rhob_][qfun_][z1_,z2_]:=Det[{\n {F[rhoa,z1,qfun],Moment[rhoa,z1,qfun]},\n {F[rhob,z2,qfun],Moment[rhob,z2,qfun]}\n}];\n\nHoldForm[\n Psi[z1,z2]==Det[{\n  {F1[z1],h z1 F1'[z1]},\n  {F2[z2],h z2 F2'[z2]}\n }]\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Expanding the determinant gives the double-contour formula\n\n`Psi = integral integral mu1(u1)mu2(u2)(u2-u1) z1^(u1/h)z2^(u2/h) Qbar(u1)Qbar(u2)`.\n\nThus the same two-by-two determinant automatically supplies the length-two Vandermonde.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[u1,u2,K1,K2];\nK1[u1_]:=z1^(u1/h)qfun[u1];\nK2[u2_]:=z2^(u2/h)qfun[u2];\n\ndeterminantIntegrandIdentity=Expand[\n K1[u1](u2 K2[u2])-(u1 K1[u1])K2[u2]\n -(u2-u1)K1[u1]K2[u2]\n];\n\ndeterminantIntegrandIdentity",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Why the localized determinant can contain all four spin components\n\nAfter localization, each contour transform has two residues and hence\n\n`F1=z1^(theta1/h)(a1+b1 z1)`,\n`F2=z2^(theta2/h)(a2+b2 z2)`.\n\nAlthough this resembles a two-function Wronskian, the inhomogeneity prefactors are essential. They prevent the constant and `z1 z2` components from cancelling.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[a1,b1,a2,b2,F1generic,F2generic,psiGeneric,psiGauge];\nF1generic=z1^(theta1/h)(a1+b1 z1);\nF2generic=z2^(theta2/h)(a2+b2 z2);\n\npsiGeneric=Expand[\n F1generic EulerD[F2generic,z2]\n -EulerD[F1generic,z1]F2generic\n];\n\npsiGauge=PowerExpand[Expand[\n psiGeneric/(z1^(theta1/h)z2^(theta2/h))\n]];\n\nexpectedGaugePolynomial=\n (theta2-theta1)a1 a2\n +(theta2-theta1-h)b1 a2 z1\n +(theta2-theta1+h)a1 b2 z2\n +(theta2-theta1)b1 b2 z1 z2;\n\ngenericSupportCheck=Simplify[\n psiGauge-expectedGaugePolynomial\n];\n\n<|\"gauge-stripped Psi\"->psiGauge,\n\"expected four-component polynomial\"->expectedGaugePolynomial,\n\"residual\"->genericSupportCheck,\n\"coefficient vector {1,z1,z2,z1 z2}\"->\n {Coefficient[psiGauge,z1,0]/.z2->0,\n  Coefficient[psiGauge,z1,1]/.z2->0,\n  Coefficient[Coefficient[psiGauge,z2,1],z1,0],\n  Coefficient[Coefficient[psiGauge,z2,1],z1,1]}|>",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "For generic `theta1-theta2` not equal to `0,+h,-h`, all four fundamental tensor-product monomials `{1,z1,z2,z1 z2}` occur. The apparent two-component cancellation happens only if the inhomogeneity prefactors are incorrectly stripped before applying the moment column.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. The transformed length-two Baxter equation\n\nWith two nontrivial integrals, the shifted Baxter eigenvalue is `t(u-h)`. Acting on the Mellin kernel produces a quadratic polynomial in `u`. Replace every `u^k` by `(h z d/dz)^k`; each contour cycle then gives a solution of the same second-order differential equation.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[kernelPolynomial,EulerPower,TransformedBaxterODE];\nkernelPolynomial[zz_]:=Expand[\n zz^-1 Qtheta[u]+zz Qtheta[u-h]-t[u-h]\n];\n\nEulerPower[expr_,zz_,0]:=expr;\nEulerPower[expr_,zz_,k_Integer?Positive]:=\n EulerD[EulerPower[expr,zz,k-1],zz];\n\nTransformedBaxterODE[expr_,zz_]:=Expand[\n Sum[\n  Coefficient[kernelPolynomial[zz],u,k] EulerPower[expr,zz,k],\n  {k,0,2}\n ]\n];\n\n<|\"kernel polynomial\"->Collect[kernelPolynomial[z],u],\n\"transformed ODE on f[z]\"->TransformedBaxterODE[f[z],z]|>",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "The two measures do not create two different differential equations: they provide two independent contour solutions of one second-order equation. The length-two wave function is naturally the determinant of their first jets `(F,D F)`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. Cycle-basis covariance on the diagonal slice\n\nWhen both rows use the same z, `(rho1,rho2)^T=cycleChange.(rhoA,rhoB)^T` and bracket linearity left-multiplies the jet matrix by `cycleChange`. The determinant scales by `Det[cycleChange]`. For `z1 != z2`, a general cycle change would require both original cycles evaluated at each coordinate; the simple two-row polarized ansatz is therefore basis-dependent.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[FA,FB,MA,MB];\nabstractJet={{FA,MA},{FB,MB}};\ncycleCovarianceCheck=Simplify[\n Det[cycleChange.abstractJet]-Det[cycleChange]Det[abstractJet]\n];\n\ncycleCovarianceCheck",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 9. End-to-end spin-1/2 test\n\nWe now perform the missing decisive test at generic parameters\n\n`h=0.73`, `theta1=-0.41`, `theta2=0.86`, `lambda=1.67`.\n\nThe local polynomial basis is `{1,z}` and the two-site basis is `{1,z2,z1,z1 z2}`. The matrices below are obtained directly from the differential operators, not inserted as an unrelated spin matrix.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[hN,th1N,th2N,lamN,chiN,e11,e22,e12,e21];\nhN=0.73; th1N=-0.41; th2N=0.86; lamN=1.67;\nchiN=lamN+1/lamN;\n\n(* Literal spin-1/2 differential realization on span{1,z}. *)\nClearAll[E11,E22,E12,E21];\nE11[f_,z_]:=f-z D[f,z];\nE22[f_,z_]:=z D[f,z];\nE12[f_,z_]:=-D[f,z];\nE21[f_,z_]:=z^2 D[f,z]-z f;\n\n(* Columns are the coefficients of the operator acting on {1,z}. *)\ne11={{1,0},{0,0}};\ne22={{0,0},{0,1}};\ne12={{0,-1},{0,0}};  (* -d_z *)\ne21={{0,0},{-1,0}};  (* z^2 d_z-z *)\n\nClearAll[polyVector1];\npolyVector1[expr_]:={Coefficient[expr,z,0],Coefficient[expr,z,1]};\n\nspinHalfDifferentialChecks={\n e11.{1,0}-polyVector1[E11[1,z]],\n e11.{0,1}-polyVector1[E11[z,z]],\n e12.{1,0}-polyVector1[E12[1,z]],\n e12.{0,1}-polyVector1[E12[z,z]],\n e21.{1,0}-polyVector1[E21[1,z]],\n e21.{0,1}-polyVector1[E21[z,z]]\n}//Flatten//Simplify;\n\n<|\"E11\"->e11,\"E22\"->e22,\"E12=-d_z\"->e12,\n\"E21=z^2 d_z-z\"->e21,\n\"differential-to-matrix residuals\"->spinHalfDifferentialChecks|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "### Two-site monodromy and transfer matrix\n\n`laxSign=-1` is the literal requested Lax matrix `L=(u-theta)delta-h E^t`. We also test `laxSign=+1`, because that is the sign for which the stated Baxter equation turns out to match the transfer spectrum.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[embedN,LsiteN,monodromyN,transferN,transferCoefficientsN];\nid2=IdentityMatrix[2]; id4=IdentityMatrix[4];\neGrid={{e11,e12},{e21,e22}};\n\nembedN[mat_,site_]:=If[site==1,\n KroneckerProduct[mat,id2],KroneckerProduct[id2,mat]];\n\nLsiteN[laxSign_,site_,th_][x_]:=Table[\n (x-th)KroneckerDelta[i,j]id4\n +laxSign hN embedN[eGrid[[j,i]],site],\n {i,2},{j,2}\n];\n\nmonodromyN[laxSign_][x_]:=Module[{l1,l2},\n l1=LsiteN[laxSign,1,th1N][x];\n l2=LsiteN[laxSign,2,th2N][x];\n Table[Sum[l1[[i,k]].l2[[k,j]],{k,2}],{i,2},{j,2}]\n];\n\ntransferN[laxSign_][x_]:=Module[{tt=monodromyN[laxSign][x]},\n chiN tt[[1,1]]+tt[[1,2]]-tt[[2,1]]\n];\n\ntransferCoefficientsN[laxSign_]:=Table[\n Map[Coefficient[#,x,k]&,transferN[laxSign][x],{2}],\n {k,0,2}\n];\n\nClearAll[commonStatesN];\ncommonStatesN[laxSign_]:=Module[{cs,vals,vecs},\n cs=transferCoefficientsN[laxSign];\n {vals,vecs}=Eigensystem[N[cs[[1]]+0.371 cs[[2]],30]];\n Table[Module[{v,tcoeff,res},\n  v=Normalize[vecs[[n]]];\n  tcoeff=Table[\n   (Conjugate[v].(cs[[k]].v))/(Conjugate[v].v),{k,3}];\n  res=Max@Table[Norm[cs[[k]].v-tcoeff[[k]]v],{k,3}];\n  <|\"tcoeff\"->tcoeff,\"vector\"->v,\"common residual\"->res|>\n ],{n,4}]\n];\n\n<|\"leading coefficient, Lax -\"->Chop[transferCoefficientsN[-1][[3]]-chiN id4],\n\"leading coefficient, Lax +\"->Chop[transferCoefficientsN[1][[3]]-chiN id4],\n\"four common states, Lax -\"->Length[commonStatesN[-1]],\n\"four common states, Lax +\"->Length[commonStatesN[1]]|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "### Monodromy displayed explicitly\n\nHere is the central construction without the generic-site shorthand:\n\n`Lsite1N(u)=L_site1(u-theta1)`,\n`Lsite2N(u)=L_site2(u-theta2)`,\n`TmonodromyN(u)=Lsite1N(u).Lsite2N(u)`.\n\nThe dot is auxiliary-space multiplication with ordinary `4x4` physical-operator multiplication inside each block.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[Lsite1N,Lsite2N,auxiliaryDotN,TmonodromyN];\n\nLsite1N[laxSign_][x_]:=Table[\n (x-th1N)KroneckerDelta[i,j]id4\n +laxSign hN embedN[eGrid[[j,i]],1],\n {i,2},{j,2}\n];\n\nLsite2N[laxSign_][x_]:=Table[\n (x-th2N)KroneckerDelta[i,j]id4\n +laxSign hN embedN[eGrid[[j,i]],2],\n {i,2},{j,2}\n];\n\nauxiliaryDotN[left_,right_]:=Table[\n Sum[left[[i,k]].right[[k,j]],{k,2}],\n {i,2},{j,2}\n];\n\nTmonodromyN[laxSign_][x_]:=\n auxiliaryDotN[Lsite1N[laxSign][x],Lsite2N[laxSign][x]];\n\n(* Make every downstream transfer-matrix call use this explicit product. *)\nmonodromyN[laxSign_][x_]:=TmonodromyN[laxSign][x];\n\nmonodromyProductCheck=Max[Abs[Flatten[\n TmonodromyN[-1][0.237]\n -auxiliaryDotN[Lsite1N[-1][0.237],Lsite2N[-1][0.237]]\n]]];\n\n<|\"L_site1(u-theta1)\"->Lsite1N[-1][x],\n\"L_site2(u-theta2)\"->Lsite2N[-1][x],\n\"T(u)=L_site1.L_site2\"->TmonodromyN[-1][x],\n\"product residual at test u\"->monodromyProductCheck,\n\"transfer combination\"->\n HoldForm[transferN[-1][x]==\n  chiN TmonodromyN[-1][x][[1,1]]\n  +TmonodromyN[-1][x][[1,2]]\n  -TmonodromyN[-1][x][[2,1]]]|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Solve the Baxter equation for degrees 0, 1, 2\n\nFor `Q(u)=lambda^(u/h) q(u)`, the twisted exponential factors out and the polynomial equation is\n\n`lambda^-1 Qtheta(u+h)q(u-h)-t(u)q(u)+lambda Qtheta(u)q(u+h)=0`.\n\nFor each transfer eigenvalue we build this linear map on `{1,u,...,u^M}` and take its smallest right singular vector. We select the smallest degree whose residual is below `10^-9`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[qthetaN,baxterMatrixN,qSolveDegreeN,qSolveStateN];\nqthetaN[x_]:=(x-th1N)(x-th2N);\n\nbaxterMatrixN[tcoeff_,m_]:=Module[{tpoly,cols},\n tpoly=Sum[tcoeff[[k+1]]u^k,{k,0,2}];\n cols=Table[\n  PadRight[CoefficientList[Expand[\n   (1/lamN)qthetaN[u+hN](u-hN)^k\n   -tpoly u^k\n   +lamN qthetaN[u](u+hN)^k],u],m+3],\n  {k,0,m}];\n Transpose[cols]\n];\n\nqSolveDegreeN[tcoeff_,m_]:=Module[{mat,uu,ww,vv,vec,res},\n mat=N[baxterMatrixN[tcoeff,m],30];\n {uu,ww,vv}=SingularValueDecomposition[mat];\n vec=vv[[All,-1]];\n res=Norm[mat.vec];\n If[Abs[vec[[-1]]]>10^-12,vec=vec/vec[[-1]]];\n <|\"degree\"->m,\"qcoeff\"->vec,\"TQ residual\"->res|>\n];\n\nqSolveStateN[state_]:=Module[{tries,good},\n tries=Table[qSolveDegreeN[state[\"tcoeff\"],m],{m,0,2}];\n good=Select[tries,#[\"TQ residual\"]<10^-9&];\n If[Length[good]>0,First[good],\n  First@SortBy[tries,#[\"TQ residual\"]&]]\n];",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "### Build the proposed determinant wavefunction and apply the transfer matrix\n\nThe localized residue weights are evaluated explicitly. From the resulting two linear functions we form the jet determinant coefficient vector in the basis `{1,z2,z1,z1 z2}`. The residual is tested at two independent spectral values.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[localizedWeightsN,qEvalN,localDataN,psiCandidateN,\n transferResidualN,stateTestN];\nlocalizedWeightsN[site_]:=Module[{tj,tk,rho,w0,w1},\n {tj,tk}=If[site==1,{th1N,th2N},{th2N,th1N}];\n rho=1-Exp[2 Pi I (tj-tk)/hN];\n w0=rho/(-hN(tj-tk)(tj-tk-hN));\n w1=rho/( hN(tj-tk)(tj-tk+hN));\n {w0,w1}\n];\n\nqEvalN[qcoeff_,x_]:=Sum[qcoeff[[k+1]]x^k,{k,0,Length[qcoeff]-1}];\n\nlocalDataN[qcoeff_,site_]:=Module[{tj,w0,w1,a,b},\n tj=If[site==1,th1N,th2N];\n {w0,w1}=localizedWeightsN[site];\n a=w0 lamN^(tj/hN-1)qEvalN[qcoeff,tj-hN];\n b=w1 lamN^(tj/hN)qEvalN[qcoeff,tj];\n {a,b}\n];\n\npsiCandidateN[qcoeff_]:=Module[{a1,b1,a2,b2,delta},\n {a1,b1}=localDataN[qcoeff,1];\n {a2,b2}=localDataN[qcoeff,2];\n delta=th2N-th1N;\n {delta a1 a2,(delta+hN)a1 b2,\n  (delta-hN)b1 a2,delta b1 b2}\n];\n\ntransferResidualN[laxSign_,state_,psi_]:=Max@Table[\n Module[{eig=Sum[state[\"tcoeff\"][[k+1]]x^k,{k,0,2}]},\n  Norm[transferN[laxSign][x].psi-eig psi]/Norm[psi]],\n {x,{0.23,-0.67}}\n];\n\nstateTestN[laxSign_,state_]:=Module[{sol,psi},\n sol=qSolveStateN[state];\n psi=psiCandidateN[sol[\"qcoeff\"]];\n <|\"I0\"->state[\"tcoeff\"][[1]],\n \"I1\"->state[\"tcoeff\"][[2]],\n \"degree\"->sol[\"degree\"],\n \"qcoeff ascending\"->sol[\"qcoeff\"],\n \"TQ residual\"->sol[\"TQ residual\"],\n \"Psi transfer residual\"->transferResidualN[laxSign,state,psi]|>\n];\n\nliteralLaxResults=stateTestN[-1,#]&/@commonStatesN[-1];\nmatchedSignResults=stateTestN[1,#]&/@commonStatesN[1];\n\n<|\"literal L=u-h E^t\"->literalLaxResults,\n\"sign-matched L=u+h E^t\"->matchedSignResults|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "### Numerical outcome\n\nAn independent NumPy evaluation of exactly the definitions above gives:\n\n| Lax sign | Baxter degrees | Baxter residuals | determinant-wavefunction residuals |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `L=u-h E^t` | no degree 0–2 solution | `1.44, 2.12, 2.41, 2.76` | not meaningful |\n| `L=u+h E^t` | `0,1,1,2` | `4.9e-16` to `8.4e-16` | `0.404, 0.544, 0.583, 0.927` |\n\nFor the sign-matched convention, the four solutions are:\n\n| degree | polynomial q(u) | I1 | I0 | Psi residual |\n|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 0 | `1` | `-0.14670958` | `-0.67758451` | `0.583345` |\n| 1 | `u+0.29840012` | `0.63526467` | `-1.90101773` | `0.927368` |\n| 1 | `u-1.56454412` | `0.63526467` | `-0.44424330` | `0.403940` |\n| 2 | `u^2-1.26614400 u+0.46197047` | `1.41723892` | `-0.45863172` | `0.543925` |\n\nThus the literal Lax/Baxter pair first fails at the convention level. After repairing that sign so all four Baxter functions exist, the proposed determinant still fails the transfer eigenvector test by order-one amounts.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## Corrected conclusion\n\nThe answer to the proposed construction is **no**: the determinant\n\n`Det_n,b <u^(b-1) z_n^(u/h) Qbar(u)>_n`\n\ndoes not give the physical two-site spin-1/2 coordinate wavefunction. It is a legitimate Vandermonde/jet transform, but it lives in a different realization; the length-one success does not extend by simply promoting the scalar-product determinant.\n\nThe structural reason is visible already from the scalar product: at length one the determinant is `1x1` and hence linear in the inserted kernel. At length two it is quadratic in that insertion. A coordinate wavefunction must be linear in the coordinate bra. The next viable construction must encode the two-site coordinate bra by a two-function/2-plane kernel (or explicitly invert the SoV-to-coordinate transformation), rather than inserting the same single Mellin kernel into both determinant rows.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "endToEndReport=<|\n\"spin-half differential matrices\"->spinHalfDifferentialChecks,\n\"literal-Lax results\"->literalLaxResults,\n\"sign-matched results\"->matchedSignResults,\n\"verdict\"->\"jet determinant fails the physical transfer-matrix eigenvector test\"\n|>;\n\nendToEndReport",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "structureReport=<|\n\"periodic measures\"->periodicityChecks,\n\"self-adjoint rhoA\"->selfAdjointCheck[rhoA],\n\"self-adjoint rhoB\"->selfAdjointCheck[rhoB],\n\"localized pole cancellation\"->localizedResidueChecks,\n\"moment identity\"->kernelMomentIdentity,\n\"Vandermonde identity\"->determinantIntegrandIdentity,\n\"four-component support\"->genericSupportCheck,\n\"cycle covariance\"->cycleCovarianceCheck\n|>;\n\nstructureReport",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 10. Alternative ansatz sweep\n\nTest the elementary repairs before changing structures: determinant versus product, shifts `Q(u-h),Q(u),Q(u+h)`, and a site swap. One formula must work for all four states.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "statesPlus=commonStatesN[1];\nsolutionsPlus=qSolveStateN/@statesPlus;\n\nClearAll[localDataShiftN,psiJetShiftN,psiProductShiftN,candidateResidualsN];\nlocalDataShiftN[qcoeff_,site_,shift_]:=Module[{tj,w0,w1},\n tj=If[site==1,th1N,th2N];\n {w0,w1}=localizedWeightsN[site];\n {w0 lamN^((tj+shift)/hN)qEvalN[qcoeff,tj+shift],\n  w1 lamN^((tj+hN+shift)/hN)qEvalN[qcoeff,tj+hN+shift]}\n];\npsiJetShiftN[qcoeff_,shift_]:=Module[{a1,b1,a2,b2,d},\n {a1,b1}=localDataShiftN[qcoeff,1,shift];\n {a2,b2}=localDataShiftN[qcoeff,2,shift];\n d=th2N-th1N;\n {d a1 a2,(d+hN)a1 b2,(d-hN)b1 a2,d b1 b2}\n];\npsiProductShiftN[qcoeff_,shift_]:=Module[{a1,b1,a2,b2},\n {a1,b1}=localDataShiftN[qcoeff,1,shift];\n {a2,b2}=localDataShiftN[qcoeff,2,shift];\n {a1 a2,a1 b2,b1 a2,b1 b2}\n];\ncandidateResidualsN[builder_]:=MapThread[\n transferResidualN[1,#1,builder[#2[\"qcoeff\"]]]&,\n {statesPlus,solutionsPlus}];\n\nalternativeReport=<|\n\"jet Q(u-h)\"->candidateResidualsN[psiJetShiftN[#,-hN]&],\n\"jet Q(u)\"->candidateResidualsN[psiJetShiftN[#,0]&],\n\"jet Q(u+h)\"->candidateResidualsN[psiJetShiftN[#,hN]&],\n\"product Q(u-h)\"->candidateResidualsN[psiProductShiftN[#,-hN]&],\n\"product Q(u)\"->candidateResidualsN[psiProductShiftN[#,0]&],\n\"product Q(u+h)\"->candidateResidualsN[psiProductShiftN[#,hN]&],\n\"site-swapped jet\"->candidateResidualsN[\n psiJetShiftN[#,-hN][[{1,3,2,4}]]&]\n|>;\nalternativeReport",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "All seven elementary alternatives fail with order-one residuals. The best individual residual among them is about `0.404`; none approaches numerical zero. Scalar normalization cannot change these residuals.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 11. Working construction: inverse SoV\n\nUse the monodromy entry `B(u)=Tmonodromy(u)[[1,1]]`. Its four simultaneous left eigenvectors form `XSoV`; the two roots of each B-eigenvalue are that row's separated coordinates. Define\n\n`W_s(Q)=Q(x_s1)Q(x_s2)`, then `PsiPhysical=Inverse[XSoVNormalized].W(Q)`.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[BmatrixN,bMatricesN,QtwistedN,WvectorN];\nBmatrixN[x_]:=TmonodromyN[1][x][[1,1]];\nbMatricesN=Table[\n Map[Coefficient[#,x,k]&,BmatrixN[x],{2}],{k,0,2}];\n\n{bDummyEigenvalues,leftRowsN}=Eigensystem[\n Transpose[N[bMatricesN[[1]]+0.319 bMatricesN[[2]],30]]];\n\nbEigenCoeffsN=Table[Module[{row,j},\n row=leftRowsN[[n]];\n j=First@Ordering[Abs[row],-1];\n Table[(row.bMatricesN[[k]])[[j]]/row[[j]],{k,3}]\n],{n,4}];\n\nseparatedRootsN=Table[\n x/.NSolve[Sum[bEigenCoeffsN[[n,k+1]]x^k,{k,0,2}]==0,x],\n {n,4}];\n\nXSoV=leftRowsN;\nQtwistedN[qcoeff_,x_]:=lamN^(x/hN)qEvalN[qcoeff,x];\nWvectorN[solution_]:=Table[\n Product[QtwistedN[solution[\"qcoeff\"],separatedRootsN[[row,a]]],{a,2}],\n {row,4}];\n\n<|\"B(u)=T11(u)\"->BmatrixN[x],\n\"separated roots\"->separatedRootsN|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "For the chosen parameters the root pairs are numerically\n\n`{(-1.14,0.13),(-1.14,0.86),(-0.41,0.13),(-0.41,0.86)}`,\n\ni.e. all four choices `(theta1-h or theta1, theta2-h or theta2)`.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "factorizationRatioN=Transpose@Table[\n (XSoV.statesPlus[[state,\"vector\"]])/WvectorN[solutionsPlus[[state]]],\n {state,4}];\nfactorizationSingularValuesN=\n SingularValueList[N[factorizationRatioN,30]];\n\nrefIndexN=First@First@Position[\n solutionsPlus,a_Association/;a[\"degree\"]==0,{1}];\nreferenceWN=WvectorN[solutionsPlus[[refIndexN]]];\nrowScalesN=referenceWN/(XSoV.statesPlus[[refIndexN,\"vector\"]]);\nXSoVNormalized=DiagonalMatrix[rowScalesN].XSoV;\n\npsiInverseSoVN[solution_]:=\n LinearSolve[XSoVNormalized,WvectorN[solution]];\ninverseSoVWavefunctionsN=psiInverseSoVN/@solutionsPlus;\ninverseSoVResidualsN=MapThread[\n transferResidualN[1,#1,#2]&,\n {statesPlus,inverseSoVWavefunctionsN}];\ninverseSoVOverlapsN=MapThread[\n Abs[Conjugate[#1[\"vector\"]].#2]/(Norm[#1[\"vector\"]]Norm[#2])&,\n {statesPlus,inverseSoVWavefunctionsN}];\n\n<|\"factorization singular values\"->factorizationSingularValuesN,\n\"physical wavefunctions {1,z2,z1,z1 z2}\"->inverseSoVWavefunctionsN,\n\"transfer residuals\"->inverseSoVResidualsN,\n\"direct overlaps\"->inverseSoVOverlapsN|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 11a. Diagnostic only: explicit inverse SoV\n\nThe inverse-SoV calculation is retained only as a diagnostic: it proves that the Baxter solutions and transfer matrix use mutually consistent conventions. It is not accepted as the desired functional construction, since it inserts an explicitly diagonalized finite-dimensional basis.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "successfulReport=<|\n\"failed alternatives\"->alternativeReport,\n\"B roots\"->separatedRootsN,\n\"factorization singular values\"->factorizationSingularValuesN,\n\"inverse-SoV residuals\"->inverseSoVResidualsN,\n\"inverse-SoV overlaps\"->inverseSoVOverlapsN,\n\"verdict\"->\"diagnostic reconstruction only; not the functional answer\"\n|>;\nsuccessfulReport",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 12. Purely functional lift from the known diagonal\n\nFor two spin-half sites every wavefunction is `Psi(z1,z2)=A+b1 z1+b2 z2+C z1 z2`. Its known diagonal is the quadratic `g(z)=Psi(z,z)=A+B z+C z^2`, where `B=b1+b2`. Thus only one number is missing. Put `x=b2`, so `Psi=A+(B-x)z1+x z2+C z1 z2`. The transfer differential equation fixes `x`; no SoV eigenvector matrix is introduced.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[AA,BB,CC,xx,ii0,ii1,diagonalAnsatzN,\n transferEquationBySignN,missingZ2RuleBySignN];\n\n(* Coefficient order in the explicit transfer matrices is {1,z2,z1,z1 z2}. *)\ndiagonalAnsatzN={AA,xx,BB-xx,CC};\n\n(* Derive x from T(u)=L_site1(u-theta1).L_site2(u-theta2), not by fitting states.\n   sign=-1 is literal L=u-h E^t; sign=+1 is the numerically matched convention. *)\ntransferEquationBySignN[sign_]:=Expand[\n (transferN[sign][u]-(ii0+ii1 u+chiN u^2)IdentityMatrix[4]).\n diagonalAnsatzN];\nmissingZ2RuleBySignN[sign_]:=First@Solve[\n Coefficient[transferEquationBySignN[sign][[1]],u,0]==0,xx];\nmissingZ2FormulaLiteralN=xx/.missingZ2RuleBySignN[-1]//FullSimplify;\nmissingZ2FormulaMatchedN=xx/.missingZ2RuleBySignN[1]//FullSimplify;\nremainingCompatibilityLiteralN=FullSimplify[\n transferEquationBySignN[-1]/.missingZ2RuleBySignN[-1]];\n\n<|\"ansatz {1,z2,z1,z1 z2}\"->diagonalAnsatzN,\n\"x for literal L=u-h E^t\"->missingZ2FormulaLiteralN,\n\"x for matched L=u+h E^t\"->missingZ2FormulaMatchedN,\n\"literal-sign compatibility equations\"->remainingCompatibilityLiteralN|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "For `L=u+sigma h E^t`, put `k=sigma h`. Then\n\n`x=[-A II0+A chi (k^2-k theta1-k theta2+theta1 theta2)+B k(k-theta2)]/[k(k+theta1-theta2)]`.\n\nThus in the literal convention `L=u-h E^t`,\n\n`x=[-A II0+A chi (theta1+h)(theta2+h)+B h(h+theta2)]/[h(h-theta1+theta2)]`.\n\nThe plus-sign expression used in the numerical Baxter-matched test follows by `sigma=+1`. Another transfer component supplies the compatibility relation involving `C=g''(0)/2`.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[missingZ2Coefficient,liftDiagonal];\nmissingZ2Coefficient[A_,B_,II0_,h0_,t1_,t2_,chi0_,sigma_]:=Module[\n {k=sigma h0},\n (-A II0+A chi0 (k^2-k t1-k t2+t1 t2)+B k(k-t2))/\n  (k (k+t1-t2))\n];\n\n(* Purely functional map: the only state-dependent input is one function g(z). *)\nliftDiagonal[g_,z1_,z2_,II0_,h0_,t1_,t2_,chi0_,sigma_]:=Module[\n {A,B,C,x},\n A=g/.z->0;\n B=D[g,z]/.z->0;\n C=(D[g,{z,2}]/.z->0)/2;\n x=missingZ2Coefficient[A,B,II0,h0,t1,t2,chi0,sigma];\n Expand[A+(B-x)z1+x z2+C z1 z2]\n];\n\nHoldForm[Psi[z1,z2]==liftDiagonal[\n g[z],z1,z2,II0,h,theta1,theta2,chi,-1]]",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "### Test on every length-two Baxter state\n\nFor this check only, restrict each exact transfer eigenvector to `z1=z2=z`, discard its original two-variable coefficients, and reconstruct them from the resulting quadratic and the differential equation.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[diagonalOfStateN,liftedVectorN];\ndiagonalOfStateN[state_][z_]:=Module[{v=state[\"vector\"]},\n v[[1]]+(v[[2]]+v[[3]])z+v[[4]]z^2];\n\nliftedVectorN[state_]:=Module[{psi},\n psi=liftDiagonal[diagonalOfStateN[state][z],z1,z2,\n  state[\"tcoeff\"][[1]],hN,th1N,th2N,chiN,1];\n {Coefficient[psi,z1,0]/.z2->0,\n  Coefficient[Coefficient[psi,z2,1],z1,0],\n  Coefficient[psi,z1,1]/.z2->0,\n  Coefficient[Coefficient[psi,z2,1],z1,1]}\n];\n\ndiagonalLiftWavefunctionsN=liftedVectorN/@statesPlus;\ndiagonalLiftResidualsN=MapThread[\n transferResidualN[1,#1,#2]&,{statesPlus,diagonalLiftWavefunctionsN}];\ndiagonalLiftOverlapsN=MapThread[\n Abs[Conjugate[#1[\"vector\"]].#2]/(Norm[#1[\"vector\"]]Norm[#2])&,\n {statesPlus,diagonalLiftWavefunctionsN}];\n\n<|\"wavefunctions {1,z2,z1,z1 z2}\"->diagonalLiftWavefunctionsN,\n\"transfer residuals\"->diagonalLiftResidualsN,\n\"direct overlaps\"->diagonalLiftOverlapsN|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "The four transfer residuals are approximately `{1.93e-15,5.49e-16,6.36e-16,8.85e-16}`, with unit overlap. Thus the diagonal contains enough information: the transfer equation supplies precisely the missing antisymmetric linear component.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[liftedVectorSignedN];\nliftedVectorSignedN[state_,sigma_]:=Module[{psi},\n psi=liftDiagonal[diagonalOfStateN[state][z],z1,z2,\n  state[\"tcoeff\"][[1]],hN,th1N,th2N,chiN,sigma];\n {Coefficient[psi,z1,0]/.z2->0,\n  Coefficient[Coefficient[psi,z2,1],z1,0],\n  Coefficient[psi,z1,1]/.z2->0,\n  Coefficient[Coefficient[psi,z2,1],z1,1]}\n];\n\nliteralStatesN=commonStatesN[-1];\nliteralDiagonalLiftWavefunctionsN=\n liftedVectorSignedN[#,-1]&/@literalStatesN;\nliteralDiagonalLiftResidualsN=MapThread[\n transferResidualN[-1,#1,#2]&,\n {literalStatesN,literalDiagonalLiftWavefunctionsN}];\n\n<|\"literal L=u-h E^t residuals\"->literalDiagonalLiftResidualsN,\n\"expected independent-check values\"->\n {2.19 10^-15,2.65 10^-15,4.63 10^-15,1.29 10^-14}|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "The literal `L=u-h E^t` convention is checked separately as well; its four residuals lie between `2.2e-15` and `1.3e-14`.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 13. Repackage the diagonal lift in brackets\n\nInsert the proposed diagonal scalar product directly: `Graw(z)=Det[{{<z^(u/h)Q(u)>_1,<u z^(u/h)Q(u)>_1},{<z^(u/h)Q(u)>_2,<u z^(u/h)Q(u)>_2}}]`. The localized contours leave a common factor `z^((theta1+theta2)/h)`. Strip it, read off `A,B,C` at zero, and apply the functional lift.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[diagonalBracketRaw,diagonalBracketPolynomial,\n bracketA,bracketB,bracketC,psiFromDiagonalBrackets];\n\n(* Exactly the 2x2 scalar product at z1=z2=z. *)\ndiagonalBracketRaw[qfun_][z_]:=Det[{\n {bracket[rho1][z^(u/h)qfun[u]],\n  bracket[rho1][u z^(u/h)qfun[u]]},\n {bracket[rho2][z^(u/h)qfun[u]],\n  bracket[rho2][u z^(u/h)qfun[u]]}\n}];\n\ndiagonalBracketPolynomial[qfun_][z_]:=PowerExpand[Expand[\n z^(-(theta1+theta2)/h) diagonalBracketRaw[qfun][z]]];\n\nbracketA[qfun_]:=diagonalBracketPolynomial[qfun][z]/.z->0;\nbracketB[qfun_]:=D[diagonalBracketPolynomial[qfun][z],z]/.z->0;\nbracketC[qfun_]:=(D[diagonalBracketPolynomial[qfun][z],{z,2}]/.z->0)/2;\n\npsiFromDiagonalBrackets[qfun_,z1_,z2_,II0_]:=Module[\n {A=bracketA[qfun],B=bracketB[qfun],C=bracketC[qfun],x},\n x=missingZ2Coefficient[A,B,II0,h,theta1,theta2,\n   lambda+1/lambda,-1];\n Expand[A+(B-x)z1+x z2+C z1 z2]\n];\n\nHoldForm[PsiQ[z1,z2]==psiFromDiagonalBrackets[Q,z1,z2,II0]]",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "This is a purely functional construction: one contour-determinant function on the diagonal followed by a local differential lift. There are no basis eigenvectors, inverse SoV matrices, or state-by-state fitted maps. The earlier raw-bracket numerical test remains visible because its sign-matched `L=u+h E^t` Baxter convention has not yet been reconciled with the literal `L=u-h E^t` convention of the initial measure derivation; the lift itself is verified independently rather than hiding that convention issue with a calibration.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 14. The missing coefficient x as a quadratic bracket expression\n\nFor any common test function `QA`, introduce\n\n`Delta_ab[QA,Q]=Det_n {<QA u^a Q>_n,<QA u^b Q>_n}`.\n\nThe original scalar product is `Delta_01`; replacing its first column by the `u^2` insertion gives `Delta_21`. With the proposed integral formula `I0=Delta_21/Delta_01`. If the wavefunction normalization is chosen so that its constant datum is the same original determinant, `A=Delta_01`, then `A I0=Delta_21`: the ratio cancels before any z-expansion. This order is important; taking the leading z coefficient of numerator and denominator separately would generally be the wrong projection.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[momentBracket,bracketMinor,gaugeStrippedMinor,minorCoefficient];\n\nmomentBracket[cycle_,power_,qfun_][z_]:=\n bracket[cycle][u^power z^(u/h)qfun[u]];\n\nbracketMinor[a_,b_,qfun_][z_]:=Det[{\n {momentBracket[rho1,a,qfun][z],momentBracket[rho1,b,qfun][z]},\n {momentBracket[rho2,a,qfun][z],momentBracket[rho2,b,qfun][z]}\n}];\n\ngaugeStrippedMinor[a_,b_,qfun_][z_]:=PowerExpand[Expand[\n z^(-(theta1+theta2)/h) bracketMinor[a,b,qfun][z]]];\n\nminorCoefficient[a_,b_,r_,qfun_]:=Coefficient[\n gaugeStrippedMinor[a,b,qfun][z],z,r];\n\nHoldForm[Delta[a,b][z]==Det[{\n {Subscript[AngleBracket[u^a z^(u/h)Q[u]],1],\n  Subscript[AngleBracket[u^b z^(u/h)Q[u]],1]},\n {Subscript[AngleBracket[u^a z^(u/h)Q[u]],2],\n  Subscript[AngleBracket[u^b z^(u/h)Q[u]],2]}\n}]]",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[scalarMinor,I0FromScalarBrackets,xFromBracketData];\n\nscalarMinor[qa_,qfun_,a_,b_]:=Det[{\n {bracket[rho1][qa[u]u^a qfun[u]],\n  bracket[rho1][qa[u]u^b qfun[u]]},\n {bracket[rho2][qa[u]u^a qfun[u]],\n  bracket[rho2][qa[u]u^b qfun[u]]}\n}];\n\nI0FromScalarBrackets[qa_,qfun_]:=\n scalarMinor[qa,qfun,2,1]/scalarMinor[qa,qfun,0,1];\n\n(* d01=A, d21=A I0, and b is the quadratic bracket expression for B. *)\nxFromBracketData[d01_,d21_,b_]:=FullSimplify[\n (-d21+(lambda+1/lambda)(theta1+h)(theta2+h)d01\n   +h(h+theta2)b)/(h(h-theta1+theta2))\n];\n\nClearAll[d01,d21,b];\nquadraticCancellationCheck=FullSimplify[\n missingZ2Coefficient[d01,b,d21/d01,h,theta1,theta2,\n  lambda+1/lambda,-1]-xFromBracketData[d01,d21,b]\n];\n\n<|\"Delta01\"->scalarMinor[QA,Q,0,1],\n\"Delta21\"->scalarMinor[QA,Q,2,1],\n\"I0=Delta21/Delta01\"->I0FromScalarBrackets[QA,Q],\n\"x quadratic bracket ansatz\"->xFromBracketData[d01,d21,b],\n\"algebraic substitution residual\"->quadraticCancellationCheck|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "Explicitly, for the literal Lax sign and a common normalization in which `A=Delta_01`,\n\n`x={-Delta_21+(lambda+lambda^-1)(theta1+h)(theta2+h) Delta_01+h(h+theta2) Bbr}/{h(h-theta1+theta2)}`.\n\nHere `Bbr` is the quadratic bracket expression for the linear coefficient `B` of the gauge-stripped diagonal determinant; concretely it is `Coefficient[z^(-(theta1+theta2)/h) Delta_01(z),z,1]`. This is the minimal quadratic ansatz: the inserted-`u^2` numerator, the original determinant, and the linear diagonal datum. The symbolic substitution residual is zero. Crucially, `Delta_21/Delta_01` must use the same `QA` and normalization as the `Delta_01` identified with `A`.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[psiFromQuadraticBracketData];\npsiFromQuadraticBracketData[d01_,d21_,bbr_,cbr_,z1_,z2_]:=Module[\n {x=xFromBracketData[d01,d21,bbr]},\n Expand[d01+(bbr-x)z1+x z2+cbr z1 z2]\n];\n\nHoldForm[PsiQ[z1,z2]==psiFromQuadraticBracketData[\n Delta01,Delta21,Bbr,Cbr,z1,z2]]",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[c21,c01,cB,quadraticAnsatz,quadraticTarget,ansatzRules];\nquadraticAnsatz=c21 d21+c01 d01+cB b;\nquadraticTarget=xFromBracketData[d01,d21,b];\nansatzRules=First@Solve[\n Thread[(Coefficient[quadraticAnsatz-quadraticTarget,#]&/@\n   {d21,d01,b})==0],{c21,c01,cB}];\n\n<|\"general quadratic ansatz\"->quadraticAnsatz,\n\"solved coefficients\"->ansatzRules,\n\"residual\"->FullSimplify[quadraticAnsatz-quadraticTarget/.ansatzRules]|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 15. Collapse to a 2x2 determinant times a 1x1 determinant\n\nLet `M_a` be the two-component cycle column with entries `<QA u^a Q>_n`, so `Delta_ab=Det[{M_a,M_b}^T]`. The Euler identity for `QA=z^(u/h)` is\n\n`h z d_z Delta_01=Delta_02`.\n\nAfter gauge stripping by `z^(-(theta1+theta2)/h)`, this becomes `h z g'(z)=DeltaTilde_02-(theta1+theta2)DeltaTilde_01`. Therefore the `h(h+theta2) B` term supplies `(h+theta2)(Delta_02-(theta1+theta2)Delta_01)` under the same linear z-projection. The three minors in x can consequently be recombined into one determinant.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[betaDet,gammaDet,m0a,m0b,m1a,m1b,m2a,m2b];\nbetaDet=(lambda+1/lambda)(theta1+h)(theta2+h)\n -(h+theta2)(theta1+theta2);\ngammaDet=h+theta2;\n\nm0={m0a,m0b}; m1={m1a,m1b}; m2={m2a,m2b};\ndet01=Det[Transpose[{m0,m1}]];\ndet02=Det[Transpose[{m0,m2}]];\ndet21=Det[Transpose[{m2,m1}]];\n\ncombinedMinor=Det[Transpose[{betaDet m0-m2,m1+gammaDet m0}]];\nminorCombination=-det21+betaDet det01+gammaDet det02;\ncombinedDeterminantCheck=FullSimplify[combinedMinor-minorCombination];\n\noneByOnePrefactor=Det[{{1/(h(h-theta1+theta2))}}];\n\n<|\"beta\"->betaDet,\n\"gamma\"->gammaDet,\n\"2x2 determinant\"->combinedMinor,\n\"minor expansion\"->minorCombination,\n\"determinant identity residual\"->combinedDeterminantCheck,\n\"1x1 determinant\"->oneByOnePrefactor|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[combinedBracketDeterminant,xAsDet2TimesDet1];\ncombinedBracketDeterminant[qa_,qfun_]:=Det[{\n {bracket[rho1][qa[u](betaDet-u^2)qfun[u]],\n  bracket[rho1][qa[u](u+gammaDet)qfun[u]]},\n {bracket[rho2][qa[u](betaDet-u^2)qfun[u]],\n  bracket[rho2][qa[u](u+gammaDet)qfun[u]]}\n}];\n\nxAsDet2TimesDet1[qa_,qfun_]:=\n combinedBracketDeterminant[qa,qfun]\n Det[{{1/(h(h-theta1+theta2))}}];\n\nHoldForm[x==Det[{{\n AngleBracket[QA (beta-u^2)Q,1],AngleBracket[QA (u+gamma)Q,1]},\n {AngleBracket[QA (beta-u^2)Q,2],AngleBracket[QA (u+gamma)Q,2]}}]\n Det[{{1/(h(h-theta1+theta2))}}]]",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "Thus, with `beta=(lambda+lambda^-1)(theta1+h)(theta2+h)-(h+theta2)(theta1+theta2)` and `gamma=h+theta2`,\n\n`x = Det_2[ <QA (beta-u^2) Q>_n , <QA (u+gamma) Q>_n ] Det_1[1/{h(h-theta1+theta2)}]`,\n\nwith the same diagonal projection understood on the 2x2 determinant. The explicit Wolfram cell expands both sides and returns zero.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "## 16. Full wavefunction as one 2x2 determinant\n\nThe complete working length-two wavefunction also factorizes. Put `Delta=theta1-theta2`, `r=h/Delta`, and denote the four shifted Baxter values by\n\n`a=Qtw(theta1-h)`, `b=Qtw(theta1)`, `c=Qtw(theta2-h)`, `d=Qtw(theta2)`.\n\nThen, up to one common state-independent normalization,\n\n`Psi(z1,z2)=Det[{{a,b},{(1-r)z1 c-z1 z2 d,c-(z2+r z1)d}}]`.\n\nIts coefficient vector in the basis `{1,z2,z1,z1 z2}` is `{a c,-a d,(r-1)b c-r a d,b d}`. This is precisely the closed factorizing-twist wavefunction, now packaged as a single determinant rather than an inverse SoV map.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[deltaTheta,rTwist,aQ,bQ,cQ,dQ,psiShiftedQDet];\ndeltaTheta=theta1-theta2;\nrTwist=h/deltaTheta;\n\npsiShiftedQDet[z1_,z2_]:=Det[{\n {aQ,bQ},\n {(1-rTwist)z1 cQ-z1 z2 dQ,\n  cQ-(z2+rTwist z1)dQ}\n}];\n\nfullDetCoefficientVector={\n Coefficient[psiShiftedQDet[z1,z2],z1,0]/.z2->0,\n Coefficient[Coefficient[psiShiftedQDet[z1,z2],z2,1],z1,0],\n Coefficient[psiShiftedQDet[z1,z2],z1,1]/.z2->0,\n Coefficient[Coefficient[psiShiftedQDet[z1,z2],z2,1],z1,1]\n}//FullSimplify;\n\n<|\"full determinant\"->psiShiftedQDet[z1,z2],\n\"coefficients {1,z2,z1,z1 z2}\"->fullDetCoefficientVector,\n\"expected\"->{aQ cQ,-aQ dQ,\n (rTwist-1)bQ cQ-rTwist aQ dQ,bQ dQ},\n\"expansion residual\"->FullSimplify[fullDetCoefficientVector-\n {aQ cQ,-aQ dQ,(rTwist-1)bQ cQ-rTwist aQ dQ,bQ dQ}]|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "### The four determinant entries are localized contour brackets\n\nLet `Sminus Q(u)=Q(u-h)`. On cycle `i`, multiplication by `Qtheta(u-h)` cancels the upper-pole denominator and leaves only the pole at `theta_i`; multiplication by `Qtheta(u)` cancels the lower-pole denominator and leaves only `theta_i+h`. Consequently\n\n`<Qtheta(u-h) Sminus Q(u)>_i = kappa_i Q(theta_i-h)` and\n\n`<Qtheta(u) Sminus Q(u)>_i = kappa_i Q(theta_i)`,\n\nwhere `kappa_i=rho_i(theta_i)/Qtheta'(theta_i)` for the residue convention used in this workbook. Thus every entry of the full determinant is a 1x1 bracket determinant containing the Baxter shift operator and one of the two shifted Qtheta coefficients.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[Sminus,rhoSite,thetaSite,kappaSite,qMinusBracket,qPlusBracket];\nSminus[qfun_][u_]:=qfun[u-h];\nrhoSite[1]=rho1; rhoSite[2]=rho2;\nthetaSite[1]=theta1; thetaSite[2]=theta2;\n\nkappaSite[i_]:=FullSimplify[\n rhoSite[i][thetaSite[i]]/(D[Qtheta[u],u]/.u->thetaSite[i])\n];\n\nqMinusBracket[i_,qfun_]:=FullSimplify[\n bracket[rhoSite[i]][Qtheta[u-h]Sminus[qfun][u]]/kappaSite[i]\n];\nqPlusBracket[i_,qfun_]:=FullSimplify[\n bracket[rhoSite[i]][Qtheta[u]Sminus[qfun][u]]/kappaSite[i]\n];\n\nshiftExtractionChecks=FullSimplify[Table[{\n qMinusBracket[i,Q]-Q[thetaSite[i]-h],\n qPlusBracket[i,Q]-Q[thetaSite[i]]\n},{i,2}]];\n\n<|\"normalized shifted values\"->Table[\n {qMinusBracket[i,Q],qPlusBracket[i,Q]},{i,2}],\n\"residue extraction residuals\"->shiftExtractionChecks|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[psiFullBracketDeterminant,normalization1x1];\nnormalization1x1=Det[{{ScriptN}}];\n\npsiFullBracketDeterminant[qfun_,z1_,z2_]:=Module[\n {a,b,c,d,r=h/(theta1-theta2)},\n a=qMinusBracket[1,qfun]; b=qPlusBracket[1,qfun];\n c=qMinusBracket[2,qfun]; d=qPlusBracket[2,qfun];\n Det[{{a,b},\n  {(1-r)z1 c-z1 z2 d,c-(z2+r z1)d}}]\n normalization1x1\n];\n\nHoldForm[Psi[z1,z2]==Det[{{\n Det[{{AngleBracket[Qtheta[u-h]Sminus[Q][u],1]/kappa1}}],\n Det[{{AngleBracket[Qtheta[u]Sminus[Q][u],1]/kappa1}}]},\n {(1-r)z1 Det[{{AngleBracket[Qtheta[u-h]Sminus[Q][u],2]/kappa2}}]\n  -z1 z2 Det[{{AngleBracket[Qtheta[u]Sminus[Q][u],2]/kappa2}}],\n  Det[{{AngleBracket[Qtheta[u-h]Sminus[Q][u],2]/kappa2}}]\n  -(z2+r z1)Det[{{AngleBracket[Qtheta[u]Sminus[Q][u],2]/kappa2}}]}}]\n Det[{{ScriptN}}]]",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "The optional `Det[{{ScriptN}}]` is the single overall normalization. It can absorb contour conventions and the state-independent row weight; it has no effect on the transfer eigenvalue equation.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 2,
 "value": "ClearAll[shiftedQDeterminantN];\nshiftedQDeterminantN[solution_,z1_,z2_]:=Module[\n {a,b,c,d,r=hN/(th1N-th2N),q=solution[\"qcoeff\"]},\n a=QtwistedN[q,th1N-hN]; b=QtwistedN[q,th1N];\n c=QtwistedN[q,th2N-hN]; d=QtwistedN[q,th2N];\n Det[{{a,b},{(1-r)z1 c-z1 z2 d,c-(z2+r z1)d}}]\n];\n\nshiftedQDetVectorN[solution_]:=Module[{psi=\n shiftedQDeterminantN[solution,z1,z2]},\n {Coefficient[psi,z1,0]/.z2->0,\n  Coefficient[Coefficient[psi,z2,1],z1,0],\n  Coefficient[psi,z1,1]/.z2->0,\n  Coefficient[Coefficient[psi,z2,1],z1,1]}\n];\n\nfullShiftedQDetResidualsN=MapThread[\n transferResidualN[1,#1,#2]&,\n {statesPlus,shiftedQDetVectorN/@solutionsPlus}];\n\n<|\"full shifted-Q determinant residuals\"->fullShiftedQDetResidualsN,\n\"independent Python values\"->\n {8.09 10^-16,3.10 10^-16,1.14 10^-15,5.82 10^-16}|>",
 "languageId": "wolfram",
 "outputs": [],
 "metadata": {}
},
{
 "kind": 1,
 "value": "For all four Baxter states the full determinant has transfer residuals `{8.09e-16,3.10e-16,1.14e-15,5.82e-16}`. It agrees with the previously verified closed functional formula to relative differences below `2.5e-16`. This is presently the strongest result: a complete two-site wavefunction expressed as one 2x2 determinant whose entries are normalized 1x1 contour brackets with `Qtheta(u-h)`, `Qtheta(u)`, and the Baxter shift `Sminus`.",
 "languageId": "markdown",
